WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.835
Michael Burry, the investor

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.103
who became famous

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.438
for predicting the massive 2008

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.173
housing market collapse

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.541
in the US, appears

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:09.109
to have

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.176
recently placed

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:13.113
a big bet against the US stock market.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.748
He was featured in Michael

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.950
Lewis, his book The Big Short,

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:21.221
which was made into a movie

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.290
The whole housing market

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.359
is propped up on these bad loans.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.029
They will fail

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:32.999
The housing market is rock solid.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.801
It's a time off.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.036
So Mike Burry,

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.370
who gets his haircut of Supercuts

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:37.871
and doesn't wear

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.172
shoes, knows more than Alan

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.774
Greenspan and Dr. Mike Burry.

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.409
Yes, he does.

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.978
Well, this time around, Burry is bought

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.679
$1.6 billion worth

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.782
of financial instruments called options

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.583
that would allow him to profit

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.685
from a stock market fall,

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:53.953
according to a filing made

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.021
with the US regulators.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:55.755
Let's bring in

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.590
Julia Chatterley in New York.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.826
He reckoned that

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:00.493
he understood

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.896
more than or certainly was suggested

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:03.696
you must understand

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:04.764
more than Alan Greenspan.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.167
He was the Fed chairman at the time

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.735
back in 2008.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.037
And he understood the financial markets

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.205
more than those

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.840
who are supposed to run them.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.541
And what does he know

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.509
that they do this time?

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:16.910
You know what?

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:17.977
He makes a big move.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.079
You're absolutely right.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.113
The market listens

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.381
for all of those reasons.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.582
And the thing I loved about that movie

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:23.583
actually is it's simplified,

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.452
something that tends to be incredibly

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.853
opaque and complex.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.955
And this is no different, quite frankly.

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.691
What he's done is basically buy

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:32.859
these financial instruments,

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.027
as you mentioned,

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.929
to protect against the downside.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:36.729
Now, you might do this

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:37.964
for a number of reasons.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:39.332
You might actually hold

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:40.500
lots of stocks,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.701
but think that the market

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:42.635
perhaps will go down

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.370
for a short period of time

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.738
and you want to protect that

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.373
so you can stay holding onto

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.241
those stocks,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.076
but just limit you make money

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.945
with these options. To protect them.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.780
Or you could just outright

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.281
think that the market's going to fall

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.217
and we don't really know.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.719
He has said and made several warnings

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:00.587
about the stock market.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:01.754
He's concerned about these

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.491
so-called exchange traded funds.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:05.091
And that's

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.693
what he's taken these options

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:09.696
on, that they oscillate and amplify

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.698
the directional movements of the markets,

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.066
be they up and down.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.534
He's warned about millennials

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.603
coming in earlier this year, Becky.

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.838
He did tweet out

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.907
or ex out, whatever it's called now.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.076
Saying Sell.

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:24.611
And then afterwards, he came back

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:25.645
and said, look, I was wrong.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.514
Remember, we then into the bull market

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:30.016
for the tech heavy NASDAQ and the S&amp;P.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:32.552
500 so the suggestion from this,

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.020
at least at the time,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.522
they may still not be options

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:36.789
that are relevant today, of course,

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:37.957
because we don't know

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:38.591
at the time

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.325
he was concerned

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.294
about some kind of fall but

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:42.795
the market's march ever higher.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:43.196
So why

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.664
you should always listen to this man

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:45.765
because he's proved

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:47.400
he's smart in the past.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.868
No knee jerk reactions,

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.670
please, based on this information

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.738
It's interesting, isn't it,

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.907
because there's a sort of herd mentality,

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:54.874
as you and I know

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.744
well enough in in the markets and enough

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.412
go in one direction.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:02.248
The rest of the herd starts chasing.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:05.218
Is there enough other

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.621
activity out there to

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.990
justify some sort of moves

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:12.825
together at this point?

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.260
Is there any evidence of that,

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.262
any evidence of further shorting?

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.331
It's a great question to ask.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:19.232
Look,

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:21.734
when this bet was made, remember,

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:22.802
we were probably talking about

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:23.903
actually when he was tweeting

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:24.904
about selling,

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.072
we were concerned about U.S.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:26.806
recession risk.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:27.373
We were concerned

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.508
about rising interest rates.

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:30.810
But he was also buying into stocks

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.111
of banks.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.414
So the difficulty in trying to take

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.216
a filing like this

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.283
and try and understand

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:37.917
exactly what

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.252
he was thinking or doing over

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:39.852
what time

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.821
horizon and based on what event

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.489
is impossibly difficult to know.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.624
And as you and I both know,

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:45.992
and this is vitally important,

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.227
there is so much passive

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.962
investing out there today

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.396
that just one human saying

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.030
we're buying this

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:51.464
or selling

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.099
that does not dictate

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:55.902
market moves to any great extent.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:58.137
So I'll reiterate the warning.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:00.106
He's interesting to watch.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.874
Don't make moves.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:02.575
Market moves

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:03.910
based on his judgment, particularly

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.311
if you're investing for the longer term.

